Embedded Operon domain extract for Zoen.

Source: github.com/enzotironi/operon @ ec7f26386171d2eec24cf49eb425e22fa9b82fcf
License: MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Enzo Tironi (see LICENSE).

This package carries Object/Link/Value Type definitions, claims/evidence
schemas, definition artifacts, an in-memory ObjectStore with optimistic
concurrency, and a compile-time section recall helper. It is a library
inside the Zoen workspace, not a cell, MCP server, or second product.

Recall helpers in `src/recall/span-query.ts` and `src/recall/section-needle.ts`
are adapted from vellum-ai/vellum-assistant commit
`4f7c8744acb4d7f4f7c6e8f1eacdf90538dfac2f` (MIT, Copyright (c) 2025 Vellum AI).
The upstream license is at `third-party/vellum-LICENSE.txt`. No Vellum daemon,
scheduler, gateway, Qdrant collection, credential service, or canonical
Markdown memory is imported.

It does not include, import, or start:

- Operon cell / Alchemy PostgreSQL cell
- MCP stdio server
- cell-auth
- CLI `--workspace` snapshot JSON
- Generated UI
- mission scheduler or provider dispatch
- package migrators / DDL-on-connect (`applySchema`)

Do not provide this package to `server/runtime.ts` until Mem0 is removed in
the same change (P10). Persistence on Zoen Postgres is a later package.
